      "texts": [
        "What the Dust Remembers Elara enters Ashfall and discovers the grey dust is psychometric; touching objects triggers vivid, chaotic memories of the town's final moments. Seeking a central source of information, she enters the Town Hall, only to find the dust inside is not settled, but is actively coalescing into a humanoid form. The dust has recorded the final, traumatic moments of Ashfall's residents. The act of touching things can reveal the past, but it is an uncontrolled and overwhelming experience.",
        "The Watcher on the Ridge From a watchtower overlooking Ashfall, a man named Silas conducts his daily surveillance. He is the town's sole occupant, left behind after a formal 'Protocol' evacuated everyone else. At dawn, his instruments detect an anomaly that isn't the one he's monitoring: a human figure, Elara, appearing on the opposite ridge. He tracks her methodical descent into the town, his interest piqued; she is the variable he was warned might appear. Ashfall's evacuation was a planned, orderly 'Protocol.' Someone was deliberately left behind to monitor the town and wait for an arrival. The strange physics may be artificial.",
        "The Ledger of Lost Names A woman, Kaelen, breaks into the Ashfall Municipal Archive, searching for a specific birth record. Her methodical search is punctuated by moments of distraction with personal items left behind by evacuees, hinting at her true motive. She finds the correct ledger, but the page she needs has been meticulously cut out. Kaelen is not an amnesiac; she is in Ashfall for a specific purpose tied to its past. Someone else with a similar goal was here before her. The town itself may be physically unnatural."
      ]
    }
